From: Yorick van Pelt <yorick@datakami.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: emc2305: skip thermal cooling path when not bound

The emc2305 driver routes hwmon PWM writes through the thermal cooling
device path whenever CONFIG_THERMAL is reachable, which quantizes the
PWM value to one of `max_state` cooling steps (default 10). This makes
fine-grained userspace fan control (e.g. fancontrol) impossible and
causes audible hysteresis when the requested duty cycle rounds to a
neighbouring step.

Only take the cooling path once the thermal subsystem has actually bound
to the device and pushed a state (last_thermal_state > 0). Until then,
fall through to emc2305_set_pwm() and program the requested duty cycle
directly. last_thermal_state is zero-initialized via devm_kzalloc, so
when no thermal zone references the chip userspace gets the full 8-bit
PWM resolution. As soon as the thermal core sets a state, the original
limiting behaviour resumes.

--- a/drivers/hwmon/emc2305.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/emc2305.c
@@ -409,7 +409,10 @@ emc2305_write(struct device *dev, enum hwmon_sensor_types type, u32 attr, int ch
 				if (data->pwm_separate)
 					cdev_idx = channel;
 				else
 					cdev_idx = 0;
+				/* Bypass cooling path until thermal core has bound. */
+				if (!data->cdev_data[cdev_idx].last_thermal_state)
+					return emc2305_set_pwm(dev, val, channel);
 				data->cdev_data[cdev_idx].last_hwmon_state =
 					EMC2305_PWM_DUTY2STATE(val, data->max_state,
 							       EMC2305_FAN_MAX);
